{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hushhush-looney-eagle","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe shrink-only complexity gate prints only aggregate counts on failure. Gerrit CI run 32914110990 reported `active=41 new=2 increased=1 stale=7` but did not name the offending symbols or their scores. Diagnosis required a separate local no-cache Ruff census plus manual baseline comparison, which is especially poor in resource-constrained CI-only workflows.\n\n## Plan\n- Preserve the existing compact counter summary.\n- Emit one deterministic detail line for every `new` symbol with its current score and the configured threshold.\n- Emit one deterministic detail line for every `increased` symbol with its current score and recorded ceiling.\n- Keep passing/stale-only output compact and keep the scanner/gate runtime unchanged apart from formatting already-computed data.\n- Add focused unit coverage for ordering, values, and no-detail passing output.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A failing `--check` names every new symbol and reports its current score plus allowed threshold.\n- [ ] A failing `--check` names every increased symbol and reports its current score plus baseline ceiling.\n- [ ] Detail lines are stable-sorted and appear with the existing summary.\n- [ ] A passing or stale-only check retains compact output without violation lines.\n- [ ] Focused tests and project CI gates pass.","id":"0ab0-6754-cc72-4d8c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","complexity","diagnostics"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Report symbol-level complexity baseline violations in CI"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787703483445883001,"uuid":"f819eb42-5532-4aaa-8ee8-0abde5de859a"}